{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QGeometricLanglands.HasseWeilBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QGeometricLanglands.HasseWeilBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WeilZeta","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Analytic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.NNReal","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fin.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Roots"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.norm_sum_eigenvalue_pow_tight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.norm_sum_eigenvalue_pow_tight","kind":"theorem","line":404,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.lean#L404-L421","doc":"**The extension bound is tight at every level**, not only at `r = 1`.\n\nOn the supersingular witness (`q = 4`, all `αᵢ = 2`) the power sum is\n`8·2^r` and the bound is `8·(4^{1/2})^r = 8·2^r`. Equality for all `r`.\n\nWorth checking rather than assuming: a bound that is tight at `r = 1` could\nstill be loose in the tower, and then the growth rate — which is the part of\nHasse–Weil that does the work — would be unattested. It is not loose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.sum_eigenvalue_pow_isReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.sum_eigenvalue_pow_isReal","kind":"theorem","line":388,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.lean#L388-L402","doc":"The power sums are **real**, at every level of the tower.\n\n`sum_eigenvalues_isReal` is the `r = 1` case. The general statement is what\nthe trace formula needs: `|ℬ(𝔽_{q^r})|` is an integer, so a `∑ αᵢ^r` with a\nnonzero imaginary part would be an inconsistency rather than a bound. It\nfollows from conjugation-closure, since `conj` commutes with powers and the\nconjugation permutation reindexes the sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.norm_sum_eigenvalue_pow_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.norm_sum_eigenvalue_pow_le","kind":"theorem","line":370,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.lean#L370-L386","doc":"**Hasse–Weil over `𝔽_{q^r}`**: `|∑ αᵢ^r| ≤ 2g·q^{r/2}` with `2g = 8`.\n\nThe point-count statement the theory is named for, at every level of the\ntower rather than only at `r = 1`. Combined with the Lefschetz trace formula\n`|ℬ(𝔽_{q^r})| = q^r + 1 − ∑ αᵢ^r` — which is not formalised here — this is\n`| |ℬ(𝔽_{q^r})| − (q^r + 1) | ≤ 2g·q^{r/2}`.\n\nSee the section note on the `r = 0` degeneracy: the bound holds there but\ncarries no arithmetic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.norm_eigenvalue_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.norm_eigenvalue_pow","kind":"theorem","line":361,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.lean#L361-L368","doc":"The `r`-th power of a Frobenius eigenvalue has magnitude `q^{r/2}`.\n\nThe eigenvalues of Frobenius on `𝔽_{q^r}` are the `r`-th powers of those on\n`𝔽_q`, so this is the Hasse–Weil magnitude at every level of the tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.norm_charPoly_coeff_seven_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.norm_charPoly_coeff_seven_le","kind":"theorem","line":331,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.lean#L331-L339","doc":"**The point-count bound, read off `P̃`.** `‖P̃.coeff 7‖ ≤ 2g·q^{1/2}`.\n\nThe same Hasse–Weil bound as `norm_sum_eigenvalues_le`, now stated about the\npolynomial rather than the eigenvalue family — which is the form a reader\nholding only `P̃` can check. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.charPoly_coeff_seven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.charPoly_coeff_seven","kind":"theorem","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.lean#L322-L329","doc":"**Vieta.** The `X⁷` coefficient of `P̃` is minus the trace of Frobenius. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.charPoly_monic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.charPoly_monic","kind":"theorem","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.lean#L317-L320","doc":"`P̃` is monic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.charPoly_natDegree_of_roots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.charPoly_natDegree_of_roots","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.lean#L295-L303","doc":"The degree field is redundant given `charPoly_roots`: a product of eight\nmonic linear factors is monic of degree eight, so `charPoly_degree` is\nderivable rather than independent. Recorded because a structure carrying a\nconsequence of its own field is a place where an inconsistent pair can be\nwritten — an instance could in principle be refused for the wrong reason. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.norm_sum_eigenvalues_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.norm_sum_eigenvalues_le","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.lean#L280-L293","doc":"**The Hasse–Weil point-count bound.** `‖∑ αᵢ‖ ≤ 2g · q^{1/2}` with `2g = 8`.\n\nSince `|ℬ(𝔽_q)| = q + 1 − ∑ αᵢ` for a curve, this is exactly\n`| |ℬ(𝔽_q)| − (q+1) | ≤ 2g√q` — the statement the theory is named for.\nDerived from the magnitude bound by the triangle inequality; the functional\nequation is not needed for this half. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.sum_eigenvalues_isReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.sum_eigenvalues_isReal","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.lean#L269-L278","doc":"**The trace of Frobenius is real.** `conj (∑ αᵢ) = ∑ αᵢ`, by reindexing the\nconjugated sum along the functional-equation permutation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.prod_eigenvalues_eq_pm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.prod_eigenvalues_eq_pm","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.lean#L236-L252","doc":"**`det(Fr_q) = ±q^g`.** The Frobenius determinant is exactly `+q⁴` or `−q⁴`.\n\nUpgrades `norm_prod_eigenvalues` from a modulus to a value. The sign is not\ndetermined by the two hypotheses carried here — it is the arithmetic datum\nthat distinguishes the two square roots — so the conclusion is a\ndisjunction, honestly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.prod_eigenvalues_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.prod_eigenvalues_sq","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.lean#L226-L234","doc":"`(∏ αᵢ)² = q⁸`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.prod_partner_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.prod_partner_eq","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.lean#L215-L224","doc":"The product is invariant under the functional-equation pairing: replacing\nevery `αᵢ` by its partner `q/αᵢ` leaves the product unchanged. Reindexing\nalong the permutation, exactly as for `charPoly_map_conj`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.prod_eigenvalues_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.prod_eigenvalues_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.lean#L210-L213","doc":"The eigenvalue product is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.charPoly_coeff_isReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.charPoly_coeff_isReal","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.lean#L192-L196","doc":"Every coefficient of `P̃` is real. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.charPoly_map_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.charPoly_map_conj","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.lean#L174-L190","doc":"**`P̃` is fixed by coefficientwise conjugation** — equivalently, all its\ncoefficients are real.\n\nDerived by reindexing `∏ (X − C ᾱᵢ)` along the functional-equation\npermutation. The existential pairing could not do this: it does not rule out\ntwo eigenvalues sharing a partner while a third has none, and the product is\nsensitive to exactly that. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.eigenvalues_conj_perm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.eigenvalues_conj_perm","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.lean#L164-L172","doc":"The functional-equation permutation carries each eigenvalue to its\nconjugate. Sharpens `eigenvalues_conj_closed` from \"some `j`\" to \"this\npermutation\", which is what a multiset argument needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.norm_charPoly_eval_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.norm_charPoly_eval_zero","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.lean#L139-L153","doc":"The same, read off the characteristic polynomial: `‖P̃(0)‖ = q^4`.\n\nUses `charPoly_roots`, i.e. `P̃ = ∏ (X − αᵢ)`. Evaluating at `0` gives\n`∏ (−αᵢ)`, whose norm is the product of the norms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.norm_prod_eigenvalues","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.norm_prod_eigenvalues","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.lean#L128-L137","doc":"`‖∏ αᵢ‖ = q^4` — the Frobenius determinant has modulus `q^g`, `g = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.eigenvalues_conj_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.eigenvalues_conj_closed","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.lean#L106-L116","doc":"**The Frobenius spectrum is closed under conjugation.** For every eigenvalue\n`αᵢ` there is an eigenvalue `αⱼ` equal to `conj αᵢ`.\n\nDerived, not assumed: the functional equation supplies *some* partner\n`αⱼ = q/αᵢ`, and the Hasse–Weil magnitude is exactly the condition under\nwhich that partner is the conjugate. Neither input alone gives it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.eigenvalue_norm_sq_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.eigenvalue_norm_sq_eq","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.lean#L98-L104","doc":"The `q^{1/2}` magnitude, squared: `‖αᵢ‖² = q`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}